**/bin/
**/*.pb.go
**/*.connect.go
# A .proto is source and is tracked; a descriptor set is a build artefact and is
# not generated any more, because documentation is read from the .proto itself.
# See pkg/docs/protosource.go and docs/decisions/0011-deployment-configuration.md.
**/*_docs.go
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite3-shm
*.sqlite3-wal

# A stray build is never source. "go build ." writes a binary named after the
# module into the module's own directory, so the root and the host both need
# saying. One committed build was 30MB of ELF at the repository root. The other
# module names are not listed here: a list goes stale with every new subsystem,
# so the CI hygiene check identifies a committed binary by what is in it rather
# than by where it is.
toolbox
cmd/toolbox/toolbox

# a deployment's default log, wherever a command was run without a configuration file
toolbox.log
logger.log
*.log
